344	+# SMA-869 Cancelled Run Ends As Cancelled — Implementation Plan
345	+
346	+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
347	+
348	+**Goal:** A run whose `RunContext` cancel token fired ends with
349	+`RunError::Cancelled` through a runner, and never `Ok(Completed)` with cut or
350	+earlier-turn text.
351	+
352	+**Architecture:** Add "token fired → return with no further event" checks in
353	+the `LlmAgent` loop driver (`agent.rs`), and the `AgentAsTool` guard rule
354	+("token fired and the child had no terminal event → no terminal event") in the
355	+four workflow agents and the MCP agent server. The runners already turn "no
356	+terminal event + token fired" into `Cancelled`, so no runner changes.
357	+
358	+**Tech Stack:** Rust 2024, tokio, `async_stream`, `tokio_util::CancellationToken`.
359	+
360	+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-28-sma-869-cancel-with-no-finish-design.md`
361	+(read it first; goal numbers below refer to it).
362	+
363	+## Global Constraints
364	+
365	+- No public API change: no new `pub` item, no changed signature, no change to
366	+  `transition` or `crates/paigasus-helikon-core/src/loop_state.rs`.
367	+- No change in any `paigasus-helikon-runtime-*` `src/` file.
368	+- Each check is exactly: `if ctx.cancel().is_cancelled() { <yield what the
369	+  step says>; return; }`. No new `AgentEvent`, no `RunFailed`, no span field.
370	+- Do not hand-bump any crate version or edit any CHANGELOG. release-plz does it.
371	+- Commit prefix: `fix(core): SMA-869 …`, `fix(mcp): SMA-869 …`,
372	+  `test(runtime-tokio): SMA-869 …`, `docs(docs): SMA-869 …`, `test(core): SMA-869 …`. Check each scope
