845	@@ -0,0 +1,256 @@
846	+# SMA-869: a cancelled run ends as `Cancelled`, not `Completed`
847	+
848	+Linear: [SMA-869](https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-869/a-cancelled-run-ends-as-completed-with-cut-output-when-the-model)
849	+
850	+## Intent
851	+
852	+A run that is cancelled through the `RunContext` cancel token must end with
853	+`RunError::Cancelled` through a runner. Today it can end `Ok` with
854	+`StopReason::Completed`. Then the output is cut text or the text of an earlier
855	+turn, and `TokioRunner` stores that text in the session as a normal assistant
856	+message. This is against the `Runner::run` rustdoc and
857	+`docs/book/src/concepts/agent-loop.md`.
858	+
859	+## Cause
860	+
861	+`crates/paigasus-helikon-core/src/agent.rs` checks the token at one point
862	+only: when `ModelTurnAccumulator::finish` returns `Err` (a cut stream with tool
863	+calls, `agent.rs:1515`). A model that obeys the token ends its stream with no
864	+`Finish` event. A text turn with no `Finish` returns `Ok` with the default
865	+`FinishReason::Stop` (on purpose, for OpenAI-compatible servers that send no
866	+`finish_reason`). The loop then emits `MessageOutput` and `RunCompleted`. A
867	+real terminal event wins over a recorded cancel in `effective_interrupt`
868	+(`runner.rs:779-788`), so the runner discards the cancel.
869	+
870	+The workflow agents have a second gap. `SequentialAgent`, `ParallelAgent`,
871	+`LoopAgent` and `GraphAgent` treat a child stream with no terminal event as a
872	+success and then emit their own terminal event (`workflow.rs:204-243`,
873	+`390-456`, `587-636`, `graph.rs:291-379`). Today the child emits
874	+`RunCompleted` with cut text. After the loop fix, the child emits no terminal
875	+event, so the workflow gap must close in the same change. Otherwise a
876	+workflow with a token that already fired ends `Completed` even where it ends
877	+`Cancelled` today (a model that does not end its stream on a pre-fired token).
878	+
879	+## Goals
880	+
881	+1. A cancel while the model streams text ends the run as `Cancelled`.
882	+2. A cancel between two turns ends the run as `Cancelled`. No model call
883	+   starts, and the turn checkpoint and the `OnTurnStart` hook do not run.
884	+3. A cancel while a tool runs ends the run as `Cancelled`.
885	+4. A cancel after `Finish(ToolCalls)` and before the tools start ends the run
886	+   as `Cancelled`, and no tool starts (agreed in the brainstorm). The same is
887	+   true for a handoff: no `OnHandoff`, no `HandoffItem`, no transfer result.
888	+5. A run whose token fired before the run starts calls no model and ends as
889	+   `Cancelled` (choice A, agreed in the brainstorm).
890	+6. A resume with a token that already fired runs no approved deferred call.
891	+   Each call gets the "did not run" result, so the deferral closes, and the run
892	+   ends as `Cancelled`.
893	+7. `AgentAsTool` returns a `ToolError` for a cancelled text-only sub-run.
894	+8. `SequentialAgent`, `ParallelAgent`, `LoopAgent` and `GraphAgent` end with
895	+   no terminal event when the token fired and a child ended with no terminal
896	+   event. Through a runner, the run ends as `Cancelled`.
897	+9. The MCP agent server returns `CallToolResult::error` for a cancelled run,
898	+   not `success` with empty or earlier-turn text.
899	+10. A model error (from `invoke` or from the stream) after the token fired
900	+    ends the run as `Cancelled`, not `RunFailed(Model)`. This covers the Gemini

